    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on **Yordan Alvarez** (75.69) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.53) as our primary offensive catalysts. **Yordan Alvarez** remains our premier start, boasting an elite 0.421 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against the right-handed Leiter; despite the park downgrade, his sheer power profile anchors our lineup. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a high-upside play today, as the 14% boost from a favorable platoon matchup and the presence of a slow-delivery pitcher against whom he can exploit his elite speed makes him a crucial anchor for our stolen base objectives. **Junior Caminero** (67.27) also merits attention, as the dynamic platoon advantage and a favorable spot in the two-hole position him as the most efficient infield play on the board.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision was opting to keep **Chase Meidroth** (44.54) on the pine in favor of the higher-floor efficiency of **Colt Keith** (59.13). While **Chase Meidroth** offered decent positional flexibility, he failed to crack the top 12 due to a projected matchup against a reasonably effective Cabrera. Elsewhere, we are monitoring the risks associated with the top of our order; **Trea Turner** (53.83) faces a stiff challenge against Ashcraft, whose elite catcher delivery threatens to neutralize **Trea Turner**'s primary value as a base-stealer, effectively capping his ceiling despite his favorable batting order. \n\nWe must also navigate the volatility at the bottom of the lineup, specifically with **Hyeseong Kim** (59.19) and **Luke Raley** (59.77). **Hyeseong Kim** carries significant interest; while his opponent Kochanowicz holds a poor xERA of 5.19, we are cautiously tracking the \"Elite Hold\" risk that could limit **Hyeseong Kim**'s stolen base upside. Conversely, **Luke Raley** benefits from an excellent SP skill matchup, providing a sturdy, high-floor presence at the UTIL spot. With **Christian Yelich**, **Zac Veen**, and **Lars Nootbaar** unavailable due to rest or injury, we are committed to squeezing every bit of efficiency out of our active core to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 Roto standings.",
